  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent pathway linking 10,17-Dioxosparteine to SF-188 through a series of molecular targets. The drug appears to act as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate. These intermediates all ultimately target SF-188, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving caspase activation and downstream signaling pathways. The shared involvement of Caspase-5 as a common target across different compounds suggests a possible role in the drug's mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where 10,17-Dioxosparteine may influence Caspase-5, which then modulates SF-188 through various molecular intermediates.",
